<title>POLAND: Optimus wants new shares listed April 4.</title>
<headline>Optimus wants new shares listed April 4.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish computer maker Optimus SA has applied to the Warsaw bourse to postpone the listing of 1,104,573 shares exchanged for 159 of its convertible bonds to April 4, the firm said in a statement on Wednesday.</p>
<p>It gave no further details.</p>
<p>Previously the firm had said it wanted the shares listed on March 26.</p>
<p>Last month Optimus received orders to convert 159 of its 300 five-year convertible bonds into shares.</p>
<p>Earlier this month Optimus received orders to convert another 20 bonds, which would increase its share capital by 138,940 shares.</p>
<p>The conversion of all the bonds would bring the firm's number of shares outstanding to 6,484,108.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
